WEBVTT

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:04.790
Inazuma Eleven GO is about to start!

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:10.650
K-Kageyama.

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:12.850
I'm Kageyama Hikaru!

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:19.850
Ka...

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:21.750
Kageyama?!

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:22.780
By Kageyama, you mean...

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:24.210
Are you really...?

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:25.180
Yes.

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:26.910
Kageyama Reiji is...

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:29.250
My uncle.

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:31.920
Nii-san...

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:34.430
I see.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.510
Who's this Kageyama Reiji guy anyway?

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:38.430
I've never heard of him.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:40.770
But why did you try to hide that?

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:43.170
Well...

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:50.660
I was told that my uncle did a lot of terrible things to Raimon's soccer club.

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:56.290
So I thought if I told you my full name, you wouldn't let me in the club...

00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:58.670
I guess I won't be able to join after all.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:03.430
Sorry for the trouble.

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:05.320
Hey...

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:05.970
Wait.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:54.310
Kageyama Hikaru, do you like soccer?

00:02:58.790 --> 00:02:59.610
Yes!

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:02.010
Then there's nothing more to ask.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:07.900
It's true that the things Kageyama Reiji did to Raimon's soccer club are unforgivable.

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:12.630
However, he truly loved soccer from his heart.

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:15.380
Just as much as we do.

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:18.270
It's nothing to be ashamed about.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:23.580
You should go the lengths he was unable to reach.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:28.850
Kageyama Hikaru, you're a member of Raimon's soccer club starting from today.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:33.240
Thank you so much!

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:35.990
I'm Kageyama Hikaru.

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:37.390
It's good to be on the team!

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:39.850
I'm glad you're joining, Hikaru!

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:40.650
Good to have you!

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:44.110
So how good are you at soccer?

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:47.090
How good, um...

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:50.450
It's only been two months since I started kicking a ball, so...

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:52.920
I'm not sure where to put myself.

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:55.390
Only two months?!

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:57.990
Oh, so he's a beginner.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:00.830
Everyone's a beginner at first.

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:08.510
But I want to become a player who can get past other players and make really cool goals!

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:09.360
Great, great!

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:20.830
He really is a beginner.

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:23.740
He won't be of any use in the games like that.

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:26.420
I'm sorry!

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:28.560
What're you doing?

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:31.820
When you're dribbling, you've got to keep your eyes solely on the ball.

00:04:31.820 --> 00:04:33.830
Otherwise you won't be able to run straight.

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:35.770
Oh, I see!

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:37.020
You're right about that.

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:38.350
Thanks for the advice!

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:46.110
All right, next!

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:52.320
Ow...

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:54.320
Are you okay?

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:58.020
Kariya!

00:04:58.020 --> 00:04:59.600
It's you again, isn't it!

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:02.800
Look forward when you dribble.

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:05.480
If you're always looking down, you won't be able to see what's around you.

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:07.730
Oh, I see. That's true.

00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:10.110
What's the point in teaching him?

00:05:10.110 --> 00:05:12.050
Not like he'll be useful anyway.

00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:14.110
I'll try it again!

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:21.260
He's dribbling pretty well.

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:23.520
Wow, he learns fast!

00:05:25.430 --> 00:05:27.260
All right! Come at me, Kageyama!

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:30.430
Shoot one, shoot!

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:31.950
Shoot?

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:33.180
Um...

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:39.660
So shoots go like this!

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:54.300
That was great, Kageyama!

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:55.510
Really?

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:57.500
Hikaru, try shooting again.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:05:59.750
Okay.

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:02.840
H-Huh?

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.210
See? He's still a beginner.

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:10.150
All of a sudden, our club has grown.

00:06:10.150 --> 00:06:13.850
Yeah, even when we were so close to losing it all at one point.

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:18.350
Somehow, it's like we're watching ourselves when we were first-years.

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:22.480
The times when Nishiki was still around?

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:24.270
Yeah.

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:31.330
That Hikaru guy is pretty good!

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:34.200
He learned how to dribble and shoot just like that.

00:06:35.010 --> 00:06:40.290
Now that there are five of us, we might just create a hissatsu tactics with all first-years!

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:47.510
Everyone, our opponent for the second match in Holy Road has been announced!

00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:53.010
Our second opponent for the Holy Road Nationals tournament is Hakuren Jr. High!

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:54.930
Hakuren, huh?

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:57.720
That famous school in Hokkaido, right?

00:06:57.720 --> 00:06:59.380
You know them, Tenma?

00:06:59.380 --> 00:07:00.180
Yeah!

00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:05.270
Their level in offense and defense is really high, and they're known for playing fair!

00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:07.810
When did you hear about them like that?

00:07:07.810 --> 00:07:11.740
All the famous schools are under Fifth Sector's control these days.

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:13.450
Well, that's the likely case.

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:16.490
No, there's still hope.

00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:19.750
The trainer for Hakuren's team written here says...

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:21.110
Fubuki Shirou.

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:22.910
Fubuki?

00:07:22.910 --> 00:07:25.920
Fubuki-san from Inazuma Japan?

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:26.990
Yeah.

00:07:26.990 --> 00:07:30.800
He's a close friend who played on Coach Endou and Trainer Kidou's team.

00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:35.000
So it's possible that they aren't under Fifth Sector's control.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:39.770
Then all of us might be able to enjoy the game fully this time!

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:41.100
That's right.

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:44.060
But they're a strong team.

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:46.660
Guys, keep up the pace!

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:47.770
Yeah!

00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:51.780
Guys! Do your best out there!

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:54.580
Kurama-senpai!

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:01.220
You're not shooting!

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:04.540
I won't lose to you!

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:09.250
Watch out!

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:18.310
That shoot had a lot of good feeling packed into it.

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:20.290
Fubuki?

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:22.990
It's you, isn't it!

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:25.190
It's been a while, everyone.

00:08:26.130 --> 00:08:27.250
Yes!

00:08:26.130 --> 00:08:27.250
Yeah!

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:28.900
Fubuki...?

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:31.490
This is Fubuki Shirou-san?

00:08:31.990 --> 00:08:33.960
I was worried about you.

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:38.680
I heard you were removed from your position as Hakuren's trainer and then went missing.

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:43.530
What happened?

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:46.460
Hakuren is...

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:50.190
Hakuren has fallen into the hands of Fifth Sector.

00:08:54.170 --> 00:09:01.310
Hakuren was also trying to prove Fifth Sector's wrongdoings to soccer by winning.

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:05.830
But they secretly infiltrated Hakuren,

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:12.030
and by the time I realized it, almost all the members were under Fifth Sector's command.

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:19.600
And then I was declared to be a rebel to the Holy Emperor's cause, and I was forced out of Hakuren.

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:26.950
But Hakuren still has players who aren't following Fifth Sector.

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:31.450
I want to do everything I can to save them and Hakuren.

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:34.250
Please, Team Raimon.

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:37.240
Release Hakuren from Fifth Sector.

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:40.810
Fubuki...

00:09:41.670 --> 00:09:43.550
I need your help.

00:09:44.430 --> 00:09:47.120
Help from the power of those stirring up the winds of revolution! You!

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:51.920
We'll do it.

00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:54.940
We'll win and free Hakuren at all costs!

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:57.040
Thank you, everyone.

00:09:57.550 --> 00:09:58.480
But...

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:01.710
There's something more to it, isn't there, Fubuki?

00:10:02.090 --> 00:10:02.870
Yeah.

00:10:03.970 --> 00:10:07.760
Defeating Hakuren will be difficult for Raimon as it is right now.

00:10:08.600 --> 00:10:10.830
Unless you can break down that Absolute Barrier.

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:13.980
Absolute Barrier?

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:18.840
12.23. Inazuma Eleven GO!

00:10:20.950 --> 00:10:24.150
12.23. Inazuma Eleven GO!

00:10:25.630 --> 00:10:33.940
Absolute Barrier is a hissatsu tactics that concentrates a number of players in the center to fortify the defense to its maximum.

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:36.950
I watched you guys on TV.

00:10:36.950 --> 00:10:39.950
Not even your Ultimate Thunder is likely to break past them.

00:10:41.560 --> 00:10:44.740
Then how do you expect us to go up against something like that?

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:50.900
You'll need an even stronger hissatsu tactics to break past Absolute Barrier.

00:10:51.700 --> 00:10:53.720
There's one way to handle this.

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:59.840
Since Absolute Barrier concentrates players at the center, the sides are inevitably left with openings.

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:04.760
Therefore, if we can attack from either side, we'll have a chance to score.

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:10.440
So our hissatsu tactics will be made especially to break through that Absolute Barrier!

00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:11.350
But...

00:11:13.630 --> 00:11:14.860
What is it?

00:11:15.610 --> 00:11:22.940
We'll need two players who both have the speed to get past Absolute Barrier and enough finishing power to score goals.

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:26.450
So that would be the key to breaking past them?

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:28.910
Speed and finishing power...

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:31.830
We've got Tsurugi and Tenma.

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:35.840
They're both fast, and even more, they can use Avatars.

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:38.040
Oh, that's true!

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:40.510
But what about you, Kurama?

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:43.060
I'll be the decoy.

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:47.490
As long as I occupy the defense, these guys will have an easier time attacking.

00:11:47.490 --> 00:11:48.900
Kurama-senpai!

00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:50.400
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:11:50.400 --> 00:11:53.310
I just think that's the best way for us to win this one.

00:11:55.450 --> 00:12:00.420
Complete the hissatsu tactics to break past Absolute Barrier before the day of the match!

00:12:00.420 --> 00:12:01.070
Yes, sir!

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:02.480
Okay, bring it!

00:12:02.480 --> 00:12:02.900
Bring it!{DADO}

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:04.140
Let's go.

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:05.030
Y-Yeah.

00:12:08.030 --> 00:12:08.890
Block them!

00:12:08.890 --> 00:12:09.580
Okay!

00:12:14.060 --> 00:12:15.370
Think you can get through?

00:12:15.370 --> 00:12:17.080
I'll be taking that ball, Tenma!

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:19.700
Whoa, why such a rush?

00:12:19.700 --> 00:12:22.670
You can't do that! You're going out of bounds!

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:24.210
Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:27.040
Oops, I went out of bounds too.

00:12:25.890 --> 00:12:29.800
This hissatsu tactics is tougher than I thought.

00:12:31.470 --> 00:12:34.270
But there's no such thing as a wall that can't be overcome!

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:36.280
Go!

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:01.000
Here it comes! Block them!

00:13:01.490 --> 00:13:02.330
Now!

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:10.220
You won't get past me!

00:13:11.980 --> 00:13:12.670
What?

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:15.980
So fast!

00:13:16.180 --> 00:13:18.480
Tsurugi, go!

00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:26.670
That was a close one, Tsurugi.

00:13:26.670 --> 00:13:28.480
You almost had it!

00:13:28.480 --> 00:13:30.040
No, that wasn't even close.

00:13:31.380 --> 00:13:36.710
You focused too much trying to get past the defense, so you couldn't shoot from a steady position.

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:40.630
This won't be good enough to make the goal.

00:13:42.970 --> 00:13:45.170
Does everyone have their drinks?

00:13:45.170 --> 00:13:46.680
Let me know if you don't!

00:13:48.210 --> 00:13:50.930
Maintaining both speed and finishing power, huh...

00:13:51.380 --> 00:13:54.020
Here you go. Drink up and refresh yourselves.

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:56.020
Oh, thanks.

00:13:56.370 --> 00:13:57.190
This too.

00:13:58.360 --> 00:13:59.190
Air mail.

00:13:59.770 --> 00:14:00.520
Air mail?

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:02.920
Ryouma...

00:14:03.620 --> 00:14:05.510
Is this from Nishiki?

00:14:06.680 --> 00:14:07.280
Nishiki?

00:14:09.290 --> 00:14:14.240
"Long time no see, all. It is I, Nishiki Ryouma", it says.

00:14:14.820 --> 00:14:18.020
He still goes around talking like Sakamoto Ryoma?

00:14:18.020 --> 00:14:19.660
You know Nishiki?

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:22.990
Ryouma and I were in the same class during our first year.

00:14:22.990 --> 00:14:24.870
You call him Ryouma~

00:14:24.870 --> 00:14:26.590
You two must be pretty close~

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:28.740
N-No we're not!

00:14:30.170 --> 00:14:31.270
Hamano!

00:14:31.690 --> 00:14:33.080
Don't move from that spot!

00:14:33.420 --> 00:14:35.180
S-Sorry! I won't say anymore!

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:35.180
Um...

00:14:35.950 --> 00:14:37.710
Who is it from?

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:41.880
Here's a picture from when we first entered the club.

00:14:43.050 --> 00:14:46.010
And this is Nishiki Ryouma.

00:14:46.010 --> 00:14:49.030
He's a striker who was in our club until last year.

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:53.090
He went to play soccer overseas in Italy when they recognized his talents.

00:14:53.090 --> 00:14:54.650
Play soccer overseas?

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:57.250
He must be an amazing player.

00:14:57.940 --> 00:15:00.550
He had crazy kick power.

00:15:00.550 --> 00:15:03.750
I lost count of how many times his shoots got the best of me.

00:15:04.180 --> 00:15:07.720
He called himself Raimon's score king.

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:09.880
Now that I think of it, he was really fast, too.

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:12.140
He's a hard one to keep up with.

00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:14.610
He was good at keeping the ball, too.

00:15:14.610 --> 00:15:17.710
Once he stole from you, you'd never get it back.

00:15:17.710 --> 00:15:18.980
Don't you wanna see it?

00:15:20.380 --> 00:15:23.800
Nishiki-san was really great, wasn't he?

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:29.030
If he were here, I wonder if we'd be able to complete this hissatsu tactics.

00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:33.640
We won't get anywhere by talking about someone who's not even here.

00:15:33.640 --> 00:15:34.790
Break time's over!

00:15:35.260 --> 00:15:35.990
Let's get going, everyone!

00:15:36.780 --> 00:15:37.310
Okay!

00:15:37.910 --> 00:15:40.950
Let's get the hissatsu tactics working this time!

00:15:42.860 --> 00:15:43.960
That goes without saying.

00:15:45.610 --> 00:15:49.240
All right, I've gotta work hard on a new hissatsu technique too!

00:15:49.660 --> 00:15:50.930
Kariya, let's go!

00:15:51.150 --> 00:15:53.040
Huh? Why me?

00:15:53.040 --> 00:15:54.520
Just c'mon!

00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:58.850
Time for us to get moving too!

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:00.060
All right!

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:01.310
Let's get to it!

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:03.910
Raimon is the same as ever.

00:16:05.460 --> 00:16:09.170
Endou-kun, let me know if there's anything I can do here.

00:16:10.670 --> 00:16:15.450
I want to help stir up the winds of revolution with you all.

00:16:16.660 --> 00:16:17.530
Fubuki...

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:18.810
Sure.

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:32.240
Yukimura...

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:43.140
Concentrate harder.

00:16:43.720 --> 00:16:46.270
Yukimura, I know you can do it.

00:16:53.570 --> 00:16:56.070
Eternal Blizzard!

00:17:02.440 --> 00:17:04.660
I... I did it!

00:17:07.090 --> 00:17:08.960
Good work, Yukimura.

00:17:09.330 --> 00:17:12.120
Thank you so much, Fubuki-senpai!

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:17.720
So this is where you were.

00:17:18.320 --> 00:17:20.970
I've been looking around for you, Trainer Fubuki.

00:17:21.590 --> 00:17:22.590
Shirosaki!

00:17:25.380 --> 00:17:27.100
You're... changing trainers?

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:34.110
As of today, Hakuren Jr. High will be placed under Fifth Sector's management.

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:38.280
So they've finally come to Hakuren.

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:40.460
Fubuki Shirou.

00:17:40.460 --> 00:17:46.180
It seems that you're a close friend of Raimon's Coach Endou Mamoru, who is attempting to rebel.

00:17:46.180 --> 00:17:52.210
On top of that, you've taught Yukimura Hyouga 
 your own hissatsu technique.

00:17:52.800 --> 00:17:55.330
These are acts of insurrection.

00:17:55.330 --> 00:17:58.760
You've got it wrong! All I did was teach him true soccer!

00:17:59.120 --> 00:18:04.270
And I am saying that puts chaos into our orderly and beautiful soccer.

00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:09.670
Starting tomorrow, Kumazaki will be instated as the new coach,

00:18:09.670 --> 00:18:12.980
and Shirosaki will be the team's captain.

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:15.650
Thanks for all your hard work, Trainer Fubuki.

00:18:16.940 --> 00:18:19.910
From now on, we'll convey true soccer...

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:23.990
That is, the Fifth's soccer to everyone, so have no worries.

00:18:24.670 --> 00:18:27.210
Goodbye, Fubuki Shirou.

00:18:31.450 --> 00:18:33.290
What do you want with me?

00:18:34.730 --> 00:18:38.300
I just came to give my greetings before the important match.

00:18:43.490 --> 00:18:46.920
This is Hakuren's ace, Yukimura Hyouga.

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:53.030
He's been accepted as a Seed and matured into a splendid striker.

00:18:53.030 --> 00:18:56.800
He'll have plenty of opportunities to show you 
 his strength in the coming match.

00:18:56.800 --> 00:18:59.140
Don't tell me Fifth Sector got you too-

00:18:59.140 --> 00:18:59.950
Hands off!

00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:06.080
You betrayed Hakuren... and <i>me!</i>

00:19:06.900 --> 00:19:08.170
That's not it, Yukimura!

00:19:08.170 --> 00:19:09.270
I was trying to teach you...

00:19:09.270 --> 00:19:10.630
Don't try to sweet-talk me!

00:19:11.580 --> 00:19:14.030
Now you're just an enemy I need to defeat.

00:19:14.030 --> 00:19:15.720
That's exactly right, Yukimura.

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:20.000
Fifth Sector would never betray you.

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:23.840
We'll see you on the field.

00:19:26.110 --> 00:19:26.940
Yukimura...

00:19:32.660 --> 00:19:34.120
We did it!

00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:35.810
That was amazing, Tsurugi, Tenma!

00:19:35.980 --> 00:19:38.300
You completed the hissatsu tactics!

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:38.900
Yeah!

00:19:39.340 --> 00:19:41.130
Looks like they made it just in time.

00:19:41.130 --> 00:19:41.980
Yeah.

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:45.260
What's got you down, Fubuki?

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:47.450
Oh, it's nothing.

00:19:47.980 --> 00:19:50.160
Okay guys, it's time to go!

00:19:50.160 --> 00:19:50.930
Yes, sir!

00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:02.090
You got the hissatsu tactics completed just in time!

00:20:02.090 --> 00:20:03.060
Yeah.

00:20:03.060 --> 00:20:05.680
Now that Absolute Barrier won't stand a chance against us!

00:20:05.890 --> 00:20:07.390
My first match...

00:20:08.430 --> 00:20:09.950
I'm so excited!

00:20:09.950 --> 00:20:10.890
Oh, yeah!

00:20:11.560 --> 00:20:14.850
Shouldn't we give the hissatsu tactics a name?

00:20:15.360 --> 00:20:16.900
Now that you mention it...

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:17.860
Kariya!

00:20:19.170 --> 00:20:20.310
Got any ideas?

00:20:20.310 --> 00:20:21.740
Me again?

00:20:21.740 --> 00:20:22.360
Yeah.

00:20:24.670 --> 00:20:27.970
It involves the two of you running through, so...

00:20:27.970 --> 00:20:30.490
R...Run-Run-Running?

00:20:33.350 --> 00:20:35.440
Sooooo lame!!

00:20:35.440 --> 00:20:37.910
R...Run-Run-Running...!

00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:40.250
That's so brilliantly lame!

00:20:40.980 --> 00:20:42.720
No way, never ever!

00:20:45.480 --> 00:20:47.390
Then what's a better name?

00:20:47.790 --> 00:20:50.410
A hurricane that comes in from both sides.

00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:53.410
How about Double Wing?

00:20:54.520 --> 00:20:55.490
Cool!

00:20:55.490 --> 00:20:57.270
Let's go with that!

00:21:17.990 --> 00:21:21.710
It sure takes a long time to get here from Italy.

00:21:24.450 --> 00:21:27.260
I'm finally back, Japan!

00:22:54.100 --> 00:22:59.670
Raimon challenges the perfect defense, Absolute Barrier, with their new hissatsu tactics!

00:22:59.670 --> 00:23:04.320
Next on Inazuma Eleven GO, 
 The Adversarial White Devil!

00:23:04.320 --> 00:23:06.110
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:15.130 --> 00:23:17.870
The Inazuma Eleven GO's proverb today is...

00:23:23.400 --> 00:23:26.410
But there's no such thing as a wall that can't be overcome!

00:23:26.410 --> 00:23:27.110
That's all!
